# Top-level HTTP module. Provides one-shot HTTP verbs (HTTP.get, HTTP.post, …) that issue a single request and return an HTTP::Response. All per-request configuration is passed as keyword arguments (headers:, params:, body:, form:, timeout:, basic_auth:). <para> /// Error behaviour follows <see cref="HttpClient"/>: 4xx/5xx responses are /// NOT raised by default; you get an <c>HTTP::Response</c> back and check /// <c>#status</c> or call <c>#ensure_success_status!</c>. Transport-level /// failures (DNS, connection refused, TLS) raise <c>HTTP::ConnectionError</c>; /// timeouts raise <c>HTTP::TimeoutError</c>. /// </para> <para> /// When a fiber scheduler is installed via /// <see cref="MRubyState.UseFiberScheduler"/> and the call site is inside a /// non-root fiber, the request goes through <c>SendAsync</c> and the fiber /// parks until it completes. Without a scheduler the same async pipeline runs /// and the calling thread blocks on the result. /// </para>
